---
/**
 * hospitality / FaqBK — "Often asked" (Villa Marindu).
 *
 * ROLE: the design's FAQ element — a narrow head column (eyebrow + one display
 * headline) beside a wide stack of hairline-separated question-and-answer rows.
 * NO ACCORDION: the design draws every answer open, and on a whole-villa page
 * the answers ARE the terms — minimum stay, what a booking includes, who else
 * is on the property. A guest should not have to click to find out.
 *
 * DESIGN FIDELITY — every value is lifted from the element carrying
 * data-component="FAQ" in "Villa Marindu Landing.dc.html", mapped hex → token
 * (R1 — no literal hex anywhere in this file):
 *   section    id="faq"                              ..... kept verbatim
 *   grid       minmax(0,.7fr) / minmax(0,1.3fr), gap 56px, align-items:start
 *   eyebrow    10px / .44em / 600 / #B99552 ......... the wrapper's .kick
 *   headline   Prata 400 clamp(31px,4vw,54px) / 1.1 / #F4F1EA, margin .26em 0 0
 *                                                     the wrapper's .h2 + --bone-hi
 *   row        border-bottom 1px #262E2B, padding 24px 0 ..... var(--rule)
 *   question   Prata 400 21px / #F4F1EA, margin 0 0 10px ..... var(--bone-hi)
 *              line-height: the design declares none, so `normal` is restated
 *              here to hold off the wrapper's heading default of 1.1
 *   answer     15px / 1.8 / #A9AFA9, margin 0, max-width 64ch  var(--grey)
 * The accent is the only token an admin colour scheme is allowed to move, so an
 * admin pick recolours the eyebrow and leaves the night alone.
 *
 * EDITABLE HOOKS (all four are declared in genericContentSchema.ts, section id
 * 'faq' — a data-field on any other path is a dead hook no sidebar input owns):
 *   faq.tag              — the eyebrow
 *   faq.headline         — the h2, set:html so an owner can place the design's
 *                          italic brass <em> anywhere in their own sentence
 *   faq.items.${i}.q     — the question
 *   faq.items.${i}.a     — the answer, set:html so an owner can emphasise
 *                          inside it
 *
 * DERIVED, and therefore carrying NO data-field: nothing. This section renders
 * no counter, no numeral, no icon and no badge. The design gives the FAQ no
 * ornament at all — the hairline between rows is the only one — so there is
 * nothing here for a display index to number.
 *
 * R2 — NOT ONE WORD IS SUPPLIED BY THIS FILE, and in this section that rule is
 * load-bearing beyond the usual. An FAQ answer is a legally-flavoured promise
 * about a property this template has never seen. So: no default check-in or
 * check-out time, no cancellation window, no deposit, damage, pet, party,
 * smoking or quiet-hours rule, no minimum stay, no cleaning or extra-guest fee,
 * no "we reply within…", and no example question. The design's own demo strings
 * ("Good to know", "Often asked") are the DESIGNER filling in their own
 * template; they are not this file's to type — note that
 * lib/derive-content-defaults.ts happens to emit the same 'Good to know' tag,
 * which is exactly why the gate below never counts it.
 *
 * R5 — THE SECTION GATE COUNTS THE ROWS, never the tag or the headline.
 * derive-content-defaults fills faq.tag and faq.headline on EVERY site
 * ('Good to know' / 'Questions, answered') while emitting items only when the
 * submission actually answered something. A gate on tag||headline would
 * therefore ship a 54px headline over an empty column on any site whose owner
 * typed no questions. With no filled row the whole <section> is omitted — no
 * eyebrow, no headline, no grid, no padding.
 *
 * R6 — blank rows are dropped but every kept row carries its ORIGINAL index
 * into data-field, so deleting question 2 can never misdirect an edit into
 * question 3.
 *
 * ROW GUARDS, and a deliberate divergence from FaqBJ: that sibling drops any
 * row without a question, on the grounds that the question IS the label. This
 * file keeps a row when EITHER field has content and guards the two tags
 * independently (the CredentialsBK idiom in this same template), because
 * silently vanishing an answer an owner typed is a worse failure than printing
 * a lone paragraph between two hairlines. Each guard sits OUTSIDE its tag, so a
 * half-filled row prints only what was typed — never an empty <h3> holding open
 * 10px of margin, and never a rule under a row that is not there.
 *
 * DELIBERATELY NOT RENDERED (so none of it reads as an oversight):
 *   · NO STAR ROW and no rating ornament of any kind. Five stars over a guest
 *     who gave no rating is a fabricated claim; that treatment belongs to
 *     TESTIMONIALS, where it is drawn only from a numeric
 *     testimonials.items.N.rating. An FAQ row has no rating to draw from, so
 *     there is nothing here to draw — not even the brass rule that stands in
 *     for a missing one.
 *   · no <details>/<summary> accordion. The design shows every answer open, and
 *     collapsing them would hide the terms behind a click.
 *   · no sticky head column. FaqBJ pins its head while scrolling; the design
 *     draws a plain `align-items:start` grid and pins nothing, and R-fidelity
 *     says the design is the specification, so the behaviour is not imported.
 *   · no onPage() anchor-remap helper and no data-href-field. This section emits
 *     no href of any kind — PAGE_ANCHORS (about services gallery location faq
 *     main) is relevant only to a section that links, and a remap helper with no
 *     href to remap is dead code. The one anchor this file DOES own is its own
 *     id="faq", which is already in that set and is what HeaderBK links to.
 *   · no button. The design gives this band no action; the contact button lives
 *     in SERVICES, the CTA band and the footer.
 *   · no data-block marker: editorBridge only needs one where two content
 *     prefixes share a <section>. This section is faq.* alone, so the Blocks
 *     toggle resolves to it by hook weight already — and keeping one prefix per
 *     section is what stops a neighbouring toggle reaching in here.
 *   · no `band-panel`: the design keeps FAQ on the page ground (--night).
 *
 * VERTICAL RHYTHM is the wrapper's. The design writes `padding:100px 34px 0` on
 * this section; PageBK's shared `section { padding: clamp(60px,8vw,100px) 0 }`
 * is the contract for all 15 sections, so this file adds no section padding of
 * its own — changing it here alone would desynchronise this band from its
 * siblings. Likewise the headline measure is the wrapper's `.h2 max-width:24ch`.
 *
 * R3 — one scoped <style>, no is:global. Both the headline and the answers are
 * injected with set:html, so scoped rules cannot reach elements inside them: the
 * headline's italic brass <em> is styled by PageBK's global :where(.h2 em), and
 * an <em> inside an answer is reached here through :global().
 *
 * CONTRAST on the --night ground (sRGB relative luminance, the design's
 * palette). Nothing in this section is below AA:
 *   eyebrow  --accent  6.62:1 · question --bone-hi 16.5:1 · answer --grey 8.30:1
 */
// `layout` is accepted because PageBK passes it to every section uniformly.
// This band reads nothing outside content.*, so it is never destructured.
interface Props { content: any; layout?: any; }
const { content } = Astro.props;

// The schema declares 'faq.items' with fallbackPaths ['faq'], so the stored
// value is legitimately EITHER {tag, headline, items:[…]} or a bare array.
// Both shapes are read.
const faq = content.faq || {};
const tag = faq.tag || '';
const headline = faq.headline || '';

// Legacy submissions spell the pair {question, answer}; the schema (and every
// current writer) spells {q, a}. Read both, but the data-field hook always
// spells q / a — that is the path the sidebar input owns.
type Item = { q?: string; a?: string; question?: string; answer?: string };
const items: Item[] = Array.isArray(faq.items)
  ? faq.items
  : (Array.isArray(faq) ? faq : []);
// Optional chaining, not a bare read: a stored list can carry a null slot (a row
// deleted in an older editor left a hole), and reading `.q` off it would throw
// at BUILD time and take the whole site with it, not just this band.
const qOf = (it: Item): string => it?.q ?? it?.question ?? '';
const aOf = (it: Item): string => it?.a ?? it?.answer ?? '';

// R6 — carry the ORIGINAL index past the blank filter. Whitespace counts as
// blank, so a row the owner added and never filled draws no rule and no padding.
// Each field is TRIMMED here rather than tested raw, because a field holding
// only a space is truthy: guarding on the raw value would print the very empty
// <h3> (10px of margin over a blank line box) this file promises never to ship.
const rows = items
  .map((it, i: number) => ({ i, q: qOf(it).trim(), a: aOf(it).trim() }))
  .filter((r) => Boolean(r.q || r.a));

// With neither eyebrow nor headline the head column would spend a whole grid
// track on nothing, so it is omitted and the grid collapses to one.
const hasHead = Boolean(tag || headline);
---
{rows.length > 0 && (
  <section class="vfaq" id="faq">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class:list={['vfaq-grid', !hasHead && 'nohead']}>
        {hasHead && (
          <div class="vfaq-head reveal">
            {tag && <span class="kick" data-field="faq.tag">{tag}</span>}
            {headline && <h2 class="h2 vfaq-h" data-field="faq.headline" set:html={headline}></h2>}
          </div>
        )}
        <div class="vfaq-list reveal" data-delay="1">
          {rows.map((row) => (
            <div class="vfaq-row">
              {row.q && <h3 class="vfaq-q" data-field={`faq.items.${row.i}.q`}>{row.q}</h3>}
              {row.a && <p class="vfaq-a" data-field={`faq.items.${row.i}.a`} set:html={row.a}></p>}
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
)}

<style>
  /* The section keeps PageBK's shared padding and the page ground: the design
     puts no band under FAQ. min-width:0 so a long unbroken word inside a row
     can never widen the grid and push the page sideways (R8). */
  .vfaq { min-width: 0; }

  /* The design's split, verbatim: a narrow head against a wide answer column.
     minmax(0,…) on both tracks is what lets the rows shrink instead of
     overflowing. */
  .vfaq-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, .7fr) minmax(0, 1.3fr);
    gap: 56px;
    align-items: start;
  }
  .vfaq-grid.nohead { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); }

  .vfaq-head { min-width: 0; }
  /* R8 — the head column is the narrow track (.7fr), so it is the one that runs
     out of room first. An owner's one-word tag or headline longer than the track
     would otherwise sit outside it; the wrapper only breaks the .h2 below 760px,
     and this grid is still two columns down to 900. */
  .vfaq-head .kick { max-width: 100%; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  /* The design's headline margin. The wrapper's .h2 ships `0 0 .3em`, which
     would open a gap under the last line of a head column that has nothing
     below it. */
  .vfaq-h { margin: .26em 0 0; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }

  .vfaq-list { min-width: 0; }

  /* Every row carries the hairline, the last one included — that is how the
     design closes the stack against the CTA band below it. */
  .vfaq-row {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
    padding: 24px 0;
    min-width: 0;
  }

  /* PageBK sets :where(h1,h2,h3,h4) to Prata 400 --bone-hi at line-height 1.1.
     The face, weight and colour are the design's already; only the leading is
     restated, and it is restated as `normal` because that is literally what the
     design renders — its h3 carries no line-height and its stylesheet sets none.
     Guessing a number here would be a divergence, and the wrapper's 1.1 would be
     a visible one: it matters the moment an owner's question is longer than the
     designer's and wraps to two lines, where at 1.1 the descenders of the first
     line touch the caps of the second. */
  .vfaq-q {
    font-size: 21px;
    line-height: normal;
    margin: 0 0 10px;
    color: var(--bone-hi);
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }

  /* PageBK's `:where(p){margin:0 0 1em}` is (0,1,1); qualifying with the row
     class puts this above it so the design's zero margin actually lands. */
  .vfaq-row .vfaq-a {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 1.8;
    color: var(--grey);
    max-width: 64ch;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }
  /* The answer arrives through set:html, so scoped rules cannot reach inside it
     (R3). An owner's emphasis stays the answer's own colour: brass on a 15px
     run inside a paragraph reads as a link that does not work. */
  .vfaq-row .vfaq-a :global(em),
  .vfaq-row .vfaq-a :global(i) { font-style: italic; color: inherit; }
  .vfaq-row .vfaq-a :global(strong),
  .vfaq-row .vfaq-a :global(b) { font-weight: 600; color: var(--grey-2); }
  /* An owner who pastes a link into an answer gets the brass, underlined on
     hover only — the same restraint as the wrapper's .linkc. */
  .vfaq-row .vfaq-a :global(a) {
    color: var(--accent);
    border-bottom: 1px solid transparent;
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }
  .vfaq-row .vfaq-a :global(a:hover) { color: var(--accent); border-bottom-color: var(--accent); }

  /* ── 900 · the head column narrows past legibility before the answers do, so
        the two tracks fold to one and the headline sits above its own stack. */
  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .vfaq-grid { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 26px; }
  }

  /* ── 520 · nothing may push the page sideways. The tracks are already
        minmax(0,…) and every string breaks anywhere; the measure cap comes off
        so a 64ch answer is not narrower than the phone it is on. */
  @media (max-width: 520px) {
    .vfaq-row { padding: 20px 0; }
    .vfaq-q { font-size: 19px; }
    .vfaq-row .vfaq-a { font-size: 14.5px; max-width: none; }
  }
</style>
